General doc URL structure

Tutorial (codelab) pages are plain Markdown generated from each codelab's
exported `index.html` by `codelab2md.py`. The per-page frontmatter (title,
parent, grand_parent, nav_order, permalink, read_time) is driven by the `META`
table at the top of `codelab2md.py`.

To regenerate all tutorial pages from their `index.html` sources:

    python3 codelab2md.py

The codelab *source* files (`index.html`, `codelab.json`) live under
codelab-sources/<area>/<name>/ (outside docs/), so Jekyll never publishes them.
Only the generated <name>.md page and its img/ folder are served.

Notes:
- The script is idempotent and never deletes the source `index.html`,
  `codelab.json`, or `img/` files.
- Parents/Grandparents for *NEW* tutorials require manual updates to their
  `yaml` heading in order to properly include the tutorial. Specifically
  `parent`/`grand_parent` (and `has_children: true` on the parent page) must be
  included. See `/docs/computing/jetstream2/redirect.md`,
  `/docs/computing/computing.md`, and `/docs/computing/external-sources.md` for
  details.
- The script only handles automated generation of the tutorial page body and
  not upper-level management of links.
